@prefix skosdex: <https://danbri.org/ns/skosdex#> .
@prefix dcterms: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .
@prefix rdf:     <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .

# Wikidata ontology layer — NOT a SKOS thesaurus. Wikidata has a genuine
# ontology vocabulary: structural predicates (P279 subclass of ~
# rdfs:subClassOf, P1647 subproperty of ~ rdfs:subPropertyOf) and equivalence
# links (P1628 equivalent property, P1709 equivalent class, P2235/P2236
# external super/subproperty). We keep it FAITHFUL — translated to the standard
# W3C/OWL predicates (owl:equivalentProperty/equivalentClass, rdfs:subClassOf/
# subPropertyOf, rdf:type owl:Class/owl:ObjectProperty, rdfs:label) rather than
# coerced into skos:Concept/skos:broader. It lives here as its own named graph
# precisely because it is useful alongside the SKOS schemes (it lets a concept
# that owl:sameAs a Wikidata item resolve onward to schema.org / RDFS / DC /
# DBpedia-ontology / OBO terms) without pretending to be a thesaurus.
#
# Built by tools/build.mjs from a one-time federated extract of the above
# predicates via the QLever Wikidata endpoint (qlever.dev/api/wikidata). The
# N-Triples extract is committed as the sourceFile so it rebuilds with no live
# fetch. The Solr indexer treats owl:Class/owl:ObjectProperty (+ rdfs:label) as
# indexable, so these terms are searchable too. CC0.
#
# NB skosdex:conceptSchemeURI here just names the graph; the contents are
# OWL/RDFS, not SKOS concepts.
<#scheme> a skosdex:Scheme ;
    dcterms:title "Wikidata ontology layer (RDFS/OWL property & class mappings)" ;
    dcterms:publisher <https://www.wikidata.org/> ;
    dcterms:source <https://qlever.dev/api/wikidata> ;
    skosdex:conceptSchemeURI <https://danbri.org/skosdex/wikidata-ontology> ;
    skosdex:sourceFile "source.nt" ;
    skosdex:sourceFormat "application/n-triples" ;
    dcterms:license <https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/> ;
    skosdex:licenseClass "public-domain" ;
    skosdex:bundle true .
